.TH PEREGOVORKA 1 "2026" "Peregovorka" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
peregovorka \- video meetings, chats and materials of your organization
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peregovorka
[\fB\-\-hidden\fR] [\fIperegovorka://...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Desktop client for corporate Peregovorka servers. Several organizations can be
connected and switched in one window; sign-in is kept as a revocable device token
protected by the desktop keyring.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-hidden
Start minimized to the tray (used by autostart).
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostics=\fIFILE\fR
Write a diagnostics report (versions, organizations, devices) to FILE and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-log
Copy the application log to the terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/Peregovorka/
Settings, organizations, logs (\fIlogs/main.log\fR) and saved sign-in of the user.
.TP
.I /etc/peregovorka/policy.json
Administrator policies (servers, allowed domains, updates, autostart).
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/peregovorka.sources
Peregovorka APT repository; updates arrive with \fBapt update && apt upgrade\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/calleograph/peregovorka/blob/main/docs/LINUX.md
